From 6a620b69cb6a387d3791d76f5dfe27400e180004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boxed-pi <boxed-pi@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:47:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Render straddling floating squares through portal
 entrances
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Portal faces lie on cell borders and are exactly one cell wide, so the
through-portal part of a straddling square is always the content of the
single cell entrance.stepped(); the rigid portal transform maps cell
centers to cell centers. remap_floating_square_drawables_through_portals
(drawable.rs) moves that cell's drawable to the transformed square with
its offset rotated — an entrance-only rule, since a one-way exit face is
not a window from behind while two-way/double-sided portals register
their reverse/back faces. Snap-family hysteresis survives straight
portals (seam coherence) and is dropped for rotated ones, matching
OffsetSquareDrawable::rotated policy. Un-ignores
test_hunter_drone_visually_pokes_through_a_portal_a_little_bit.
